From 1b3a183146cf143fd7a66fdfeaca22cb243fd64b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan3DSMods <349040779+Ryan3DSMods@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:41:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] Nintendo 3DS port: toolchain integration and platform
 layer (WIP)

Cross-compiles OpenRCT2 for the New Nintendo 3DS with devkitARM/libctru.
All changes are guarded by NINTENDO_3DS (CMake) / __3DS__ (source) and
leave other platforms untouched.

- CMake: NINTENDO_3DS branch (network/HTTP/TTF/OpenGL/FLAC/Vorbis/scripting
  off, no CLI target, no IPO, non-PIC, -Wno-error), .3dsx packaging via
  ctr_create_3dsx, link libiconv + FriBidi instead of ICU.
- Align int32_t/uint32_t with 'int' on arm-none-eabi (the toolchain's
  'long int' breaks std::clamp & co. at hundreds of call sites).
- Platform.3DS.cpp: SD-card paths under sdmc:/3ds/openrct2/, system
  language/region mapping, console bring-up (CPU speed-up, RomFS, CFGU),
  2 MiB main stack, 8 MiB linear heap.
- String.cpp: UTF-8/UTF-32 conversion and code pages via libiconv;
  RTL text via FriBidi.
- UI: game window on the bottom (touch) screen at 320x240, SDL software
  renderer, top-screen text console for logs, no terminal REPL, 3DS
  IPlatformUiContext without native dialogs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
